If $K$ is not bounded below, we can't use the given reference. In that case, we chooses a complex $K^\bullet $ representing $K$ and a free two-term resolution $0 \to F^{-1} \to F^0 \to A_ f \to 0$ (see above). Then we get a double complex with terms $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(F^{-q}, K^ p)$ whose totalization computes $R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (A_ f, K)$. The second spectral sequence associated to this double complex (Homology, Section <a href="/tag/012X" data-tag="012X">12.25</a>) gives us what we want. Details omitted.